---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolOverlap
---@field tool_a string First tool of the pair (lexicographic order).
---@field tool_b string Second tool of the pair.
---@field contested_calls number Sum over shared clusters of the smaller tool's calls: the volume both tools plausibly compete for.
---@field sessions_with_both number Sampled sessions that called both tools. High relative to sessions_with_either suggests the pair is a workflow, not confusion.
---@field sessions_with_either number Sampled sessions that called at least one of the pair.
---@field top_cluster_id number The cluster contributing the most contested calls for this pair.

---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivot
---@field tool string Effective MCP tool name.
---@field call_count number Intent-attributed calls to this tool across the sampled corpus, counting every cluster the run produced — including clusters the snapshot's cluster cap left out.
---@field error_count number Errored attributed calls across the corpus.
---@field session_count number Sampled sessions with at least one intent-attributed call to this tool. Same population as call_count.
---@field contested_score number|distilled.Null Call-weighted mean routing entropy of the clusters this tool serves, 0-1. High means the tool's intents are regularly split with other tools. Null when the tool has no attributed calls.
---@field advertised_sessions number Sampled sessions whose tools-list catalog included this tool. Only sessions with an observed $mcp_tools_list event count.
---@field called_when_advertised number Of the advertised sessions, how many actually called the tool.
---@field discovery_rate_pct number|distilled.Null called_when_advertised / advertised_sessions as a percentage. Null when the tool was advertised in fewer than 5 sampled sessions, which is not enough signal to compute a rate.
---@field description string|distilled.Null Latest description observed for the tool (clipped to 512 characters). Null when calls never carried one.
---@field n_clusters_served number How many intent clusters this tool serves in total, before the per-tool entry cap. Compare against len(clusters) to tell whether the entry list below is complete.
---@field clusters posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivotClustersList Intent clusters this tool serves, by call volume desc, capped at 20 and limited to clusters the snapshot carries. Use n_clusters_served for the true count.

---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivotClusterEntry
---@field cluster_id number Cluster this entry refers to, within the snapshot. The cluster's own label, totals, and entropy live on that cluster — join on this id rather than expecting them here.
---@field calls number Calls routed to this tool for this intent cluster.
---@field capture_pct number Share of the cluster's calls this tool captured, 0-100. Low capture on a well-fitting description suggests agents are not finding the tool for this intent.
---@field rank number This tool's position in the cluster's tool distribution; 1 is the cluster's top tool.
---@field description_fit number|distilled.Null Cosine similarity between the tool's description embedding and the cluster centroid, -1 to 1. Null when no description has been captured for the tool.
---@field top_competitor posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivotCompetitor|distilled.Null The strongest other tool in this cluster. Null when this tool is the only one.

---Intent clusters this tool serves, by call volume desc, capped at 20 and limited to clusters the snapshot carries. Use n_clusters_served for the true count.
---@alias posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivotClustersList posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivotClusterEntry[]

---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.MCPToolPivotCompetitor
---@field tool string The other tool with the largest share of this cluster's calls.
---@field pct number That competitor's share of the cluster's calls, 0-100.

