---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.McpAnalyticsSessionsActivityOverviewRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field filter_test_accounts? boolean Whether to also apply the project's internal and test user filters (its test_account_filters setting) on top of `properties`.
---@field properties? string Property filters that narrow the underlying $mcp_tool_call events, JSON-encoded. A list of event, person, or session property filters, each with key, value, operator, and type. Example: [{"key": "$mcp_tool_name", "value": ["query_run"], "operator": "exact", "type": "event"}]
---@field refresh? boolean Compute the overview again instead of serving the cached result, at most once every 5 seconds. The fresh result replaces the cached one.

---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.McpAnalyticsSessionsIntentDigestRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.

---@class posthog.mcp_analytics.McpAnalyticsSessionsToolCallsRequest
---@field project_id string Project ID of the project you're trying to access. To find the ID of the project, make a call to /api/projects/.
---@field id string A UUID string identifying this mcp analytics submission.
---@field date_from? string Absolute ISO timestamp lower bound for the event scan — pass the session's start so older sessions resolve. Defaults to a 7-day lookback when omitted or unparseable.
---@field filter_test_accounts? boolean Whether to also apply the project's internal and test user filters (its test_account_filters setting) on top of `properties`.
---@field limit? number Maximum tool calls to return per page (1–500). Defaults to 500 — the whole page — so a session's calls come back in one request; pass a smaller value for a lighter response. Values above the cap are rejected.
---@field offset? number Number of tool calls to skip before returning results. Combine with limit to page through a session's calls; the response's has_next flag indicates whether more remain.
---@field properties? string Property filters that narrow the underlying $mcp_tool_call events, JSON-encoded. A list of event, person, or session property filters, each with key, value, operator, and type. Example: [{"key": "$mcp_tool_name", "value": ["query_run"], "operator": "exact", "type": "event"}]

